s and the docs/proposal.md update.\n\n## Open issues\n- The scope is large: about four PRs of roughly 1k lines each, in a fixed order. A single worker run (60m timeout) is unlikely to deliver all of it. A maintainer may want to split it into four sub-issues (snapshot model, read-only TUI, pause and slot keys, approval key). If it stays as one issue, the engineer plan should limit this run to the first slice.\n- This adds a new user-visible mode, new serve flags and probably a new pure-Go TUI dependency. There are no product-manager, architect, designer or documentation-planner triage roles here, so a maintainer should check the plan's choices on the library, flags and log file location.\n- The approval key runs the operator's own gh as a subprocess, and pause or unpause writes or removes the pause file. Both are new side effects, so the change needs careful review against the effect layer and dry-run.\n\nRequested next: `ard:triage:engineer`\nOutput: [.ard/407/triage-lead.md](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/91686b1262a7ded2566e7d2f1f90c6d75039d486/.ard/407/triage-lead.md) · log [.ard/407/logs/triage-lead-20261125T132500.056Z.log](https://github.com/albertcbrown/ard/blob/91686b1262a7ded2566e7d2f1f90c6d75039d486/.ard/407/logs/triage-lead-20261125T132500.056Z.log) · job `01M89E31044N14THH1C8ZB34XB` · attempt 1\n\n\n.ard:\n138\n142\n157\n158\n159\n160\n161\n165\n168\n174\n178\n184\n194\n203\n204\n205\n212\n213\n215\n216\n217\n221\n222\n223\n224\n227\n231\n236\n237\n238\n239\n241\n242\n243\n244\n247\n252\n254\n255\n267\n268\n276\n277\n292\n293\n297\n298\n299\n300\n301\n302\n304\n305\n306\n307\n312\n313\n314\n315\n316\n317\n318\n322\n323\n332\n333\n334\n335\n336\n337\n338\n339\n340\n344\n345\n346\n347\n349\n350\n355\n357\n366\n384\n385\n394\n396\n40\n402\n406\n407\n41\n42\n43\n44\n45\n47\n48\n49\n50\n51\n52\n56\n58\n59\n61\n89\nconfig.yaml\nreviewers\nscanners\ntriage\nworkers\n\n.ard/407:\ncosts\nlogs\ntriage-lead.md\n# ard configuration for albertcbrown/ard (dogfooding). Started from `ard init`'s\n# template; human-owned. ard serve reads it from origin/main.\n# Anything unset takes its built-in default (docs/proposal.md, Configuration).\n# Validate with `ard config check`. ard serve reads this file from origin/main.\n\n# label: only issues a maintainer labels for triage enter the pipeline.\n# all: every human-filed issue enters.\nintake: { mode: label }\n\n# Loop poll intervals. Unset loops keep their defaults (scanners 4h, triage\n# 15m, workers 5m, reviewers 5m, prwatch 5m); 1m is the minimum. The merger\n# is controller code with no agent or job slot, so a short interval costs only\n# GitHub API reads and gets reviewed PRs merged sooner.\nintervals: { merger: 1m }\n\nmerge:\n  # A PR touching any of these waits for a human approval. There is no\n  # built-in list: removing an entry removes its gate. An entry ending in /\n  # is a directory prefix; anything else is a glob (quote globs starting with *).\n  protected_paths:\n    - .github/\n    - .ard/config.yaml\n    - .ard/scanners/\n    - .ard/triage/\n    - .ard/workers/\n    - .ard/reviewers/\n    - \"**/CODEOWNERS\"\n    # Agent instructions a PR could plant to steer later agents.\n    - CLAUDE.md\n    - \"**/CLAUDE.md\"\n    - AGENTS.md\n    - \"**/AGENTS.md\"\n    - .claude/\n    - .mcp.json\n    # What builds, signs and deploys ard itself (docs/proposal.md, Delivery).\n    - \"Jenkinsfile*\"\n    - Dockerfile\n    - .dockerignore\n    - deploy/\n\noverrides:\n  scanners/cve: { every: 6h, max_open: 10, group_size: 1, autoclose: true }\n  # Phase 1 agent roles (the ard init starter set, #39 Gate 2).\n  triage/lead:  { model: claude-opus-5-5, timeout: 15m }\n  triage/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }\n  workers/engineer: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5, timeout: 60m, tests: make lint test }\n  reviewers/eng-review: { model: claude-sonnet-5-5 }","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Hoj1njQJVoxSdn